  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD Zimbabwe Integral Ecology Programme Model (IEPM) Development costs.

The Integral Ecology Programme Model is CAFOD&#x2019;s means of embedding Integral Ecology in all CAFOD programming areas. Integral Ecology helps CAFOD to see and understand that everything is connected, and that the heart of CAFOD&#x2019;s work is responding to the inseparable cry of the earth and the cry of the poor.

The IEPM model will impact all aspects of CAFOD. It will change the way CAFOD designs, monitor, evidence, evaluate and resource its programmes, and integrate finance and funding systems. It will contribute to improved internal communication, learning and engagement, greater coherence between IP and supporter-facing teams, and greater integration of critical aspects of CAFOD&#x2019;s work such as safeguarding, gender and environmental impact.</narrative>
  </description>
